IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc5-logic`
IMPORT `ssc5-part7`
IMPORT `ssc5-part10`

-- Tests for ssc5-part10.l4 (ss 148 to 150).  Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- section named beside it, before the run.

§ `Tests -- Part X`

§§ `s 150(4) the relevant week`

-- "the week beginning with the first Monday in December".
-- 1 December 2024 was a Sunday, so the first Monday is 2 December 2024.
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2024 NOTHING)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 2 12 2024
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2024 NOTHING)'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 8 12 2024
-- 1 December 2025 was a Monday: it is itself the first Monday.
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2025 NOTHING)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2025 NOTHING)'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2025
-- 1 December 2026 is a Tuesday, so the first Monday is 7 December 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2026 NOTHING)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2026
-- 1 December 2023 was a Friday, so the first Monday is 4 December 2023.
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2023 NOTHING)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 4 12 2023
-- "or such other week as may be specified in an order": the order's week is the relevant week.
#ASSERT (`s 150(4) the relevant week` 2024 (JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 9 12 2024, `the last day` IS Date 15 12 2024)))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 9 12 2024

§§ `s 149(1) and s 148(1)(a) -- the places`

#ASSERT `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` `s 149(1) the Channel Islands` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` `s 149(1) the Isle of Man` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` `s 149(1) Gibraltar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 148(1)(a) an EEA state` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 148(1)(a) Switzerland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 149(1) Gibraltar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 149(1) the Isle of Man` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 149(1) the Channel Islands` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 148(1) -- the person's own entitlement`

-- Present in the UK in the week, entitled to a qualifying benefit for a period including a day of it,
-- and the Administration Act allows: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Treated as entitled (s 149) is enough for paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 148(1)(a) an EEA state` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- In Gibraltar (treated as part of the UK by s 149(1)).
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 149(1) Gibraltar` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither entitled nor treated as entitled: outside the limit of the grant, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A place the paragraph does not name: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "subject to ... section 1 of the Administration Act": the provision does not allow the payment.
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `s 148(1)(a) Switzerland` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 148(2ZA) -- armed forces independence payment`

#ASSERT `s 148(2ZA) the provision to which the entitlement is subject` TRUE EQUALS `s 148(2ZA) article 43 of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`
#ASSERT `s 148(2ZA) the provision to which the entitlement is subject` FALSE EQUALS `s 148(1) section 1 of the Administration Act`

§§ `s 148(2) -- the other member of a couple`

-- 2024: the relevant week is 2 to 8 December, so the last day is 8 December 2024.
`s 148(2) test couple` MEANS Couple WITH
    `one member` IS Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1955
        `sex` IS Man
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2021
    `the other member` IS Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 8 12 1959
        `sex` IS Woman
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 8 12 2024
    `married to each other` IS TRUE
    `civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
    `members of the same household` IS TRUE
    `living together as if married or civil partners` IS FALSE

`s 148(2) test couple, other member one day late` MEANS Couple WITH
    `one member` IS `s 148(2) test couple`'s `one member`
    `the other member` IS Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 9 12 1959
        `sex` IS Woman
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 9 12 2024
    `married to each other` IS TRUE
    `civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
    `members of the same household` IS TRUE
    `living together as if married or civil partners` IS FALSE

-- Arguments, in order: own entitlement under (1); the couple answer; the couple; the two qualifying-age dates;
-- the other member's place; the last day of the relevant week; (c)(i) increase; (c)(ii) only state pension credit.
-- Both reached pensionable age by the end of the week (the other exactly on its last day), other member in
-- the UK, increase payable: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The other member reaches pensionable age on 9 December 2024, one day after the week ends: paragraph (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple, other member one day late` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 9 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither (c)(i) nor (c)(ii): paragraph (c) fails.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c)(ii): the only qualifying benefit is state pension credit, so (2A) substitutes the qualifying age for
-- pensionable age in (a): the qualifying-age dates govern.  Both on or before 8 December 2024: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple, other member one day late` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Same case, but the other member's qualifying age is reached on 9 December 2024: (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 9 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The other member in a place the paragraph does not name: (b) is NOTHING, never turned into FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The other member in somewhere else AND paragraph (c) failing: a known FALSE beats the unknown.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` (Date 8 12 2024) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a member of a couple (the couple answer is JUST FALSE), or not entitled under (1): the relative clause fails.
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) `s 148(2) test couple` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 8 12 2024) `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` (Date 8 12 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 148(3), s 148(5) -- amount and one sum only`

#ASSERT `s 148(3)(a) who makes the payment` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`
#ASSERT `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` (JUST 15) EQUALS JUST 15
-- 10.01 is larger than 10; an order naming exactly 10 leaves the payment at 10; 9 is not "a larger sum" and the
-- text does not say what the payment is then (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` (JUST 10.01) EQUALS JUST 10.01
#ASSERT `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` (JUST 9) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 148(5) a further sum is payable in respect of the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 148(5) a further sum is payable in respect of the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 149(2) to (6) -- supplementary provisions`

-- (2)(a): a benefit other than state pension credit, entitled but for another public payment.
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the person is treated as entitled to a payment of the qualifying benefit` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2)(b): state pension credit, entitlement lost through exceptional income.
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the person is treated as entitled to a payment of the qualifying benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The wrong limb for the benefit: for state pension credit the other-payment limb does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the person is treated as entitled to a payment of the qualifying benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- For a benefit other than state pension credit the exceptional-income limb does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the person is treated as entitled to a payment of the qualifying benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the person is treated as entitled to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the person is treated as entitled to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the person is treated as entitled to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): a war disablement pension and pensionable age reached after the end of the relevant week (8 Dec 2024).
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the person is entitled to a payment of the war disablement pension` TRUE (Date 9 12 2024) (Date 8 12 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the person is entitled to a payment of the war disablement pension` TRUE (Date 8 12 2024) (Date 8 12 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the person is entitled to a payment of the war disablement pension` FALSE (Date 9 12 2024) (Date 8 12 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(5) the sum is treated as benefit for the purposes of the enactment or instrument under which entitlement to the qualifying benefit arises` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(5) the sum is treated as benefit for the purposes of the enactment or instrument under which entitlement to the qualifying benefit arises` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the payment and the right to receive it are disregarded` TRUE `s 149(6) for the purposes of income tax` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the payment and the right to receive it are disregarded` TRUE `s 149(6) for the purposes of an enactment or instrument under which regard is had to a person's means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the payment and the right to receive it are disregarded` TRUE `s 149(6) for some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the payment and the right to receive it are disregarded` FALSE `s 149(6) for the purposes of income tax` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 150 -- interpretation of Part X`

#ASSERT `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `s 150(1)(a) a retirement pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `s 150(1)(l) a mobility supplement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `s 150(1)(k) state pension credit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `s 150(1)(c) a widowed mother's allowance, widowed parent's allowance or widow's pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `s 150(1) a payment of some other kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a retirement pension` `s 150(2) a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a retirement pension` `s 150(2) graduated retirement benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a retirement pension` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of pension` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the allowance is a qualifying employment and support allowance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the allowance is a qualifying employment and support allowance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the allowance is a qualifying employment and support allowance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the supplement is a mobility supplement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the supplement is a mobility supplement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the supplement is a mobility supplement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an attendance allowance` `s 150(2) a disability living allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an attendance allowance` `s 150(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an attendance allowance` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of attendance payment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an attendance allowance` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of attendance payment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an unemployability supplement or allowance` `s 150(2) an unemployability supplement payable under Part I of Schedule 7` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an unemployability supplement or allowance` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of unemployability payment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is an unemployability supplement or allowance` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of unemployability payment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a war disablement pension` `s 150(2) retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a war disablement pension` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war disablement pension` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a war disablement pension` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war disablement pension` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a war widow's pension` `s 150(2) a pension or allowance for a widow or surviving civil partner granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is a war widow's pension` `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war widow's pension` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) pensionable age`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) state pension credit`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) adult disability payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) armed forces independence payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) carer support payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
-- "the qualifying age for state pension credit" (s 150(2)) is s 137(1)'s: a woman's pensionable age; a man's is
-- the date a woman born on his birthday attains it.
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the date the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` (`s 148(2) test couple`'s `the other member`) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 8 12 2024
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the date the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` (`s 148(2) test couple`'s `one member`) (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS Date 1 3 2023
-- s 150(3): "couple" has the meaning in s 137(1).
#ASSERT `s 150(3) the two persons are a couple` `s 148(2) test couple` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 148(2A) and the closing words of s 150(2)`

-- (2A): where the only qualifying benefit is state pension credit, paragraph (a) of subsection (2) reads the
-- qualifying age for state pension credit; in every other case it reads pensionable age.
#ASSERT `s 148(2A) the age that paragraph (a) of subsection (2) reads` TRUE EQUALS `s 148(2A) the qualifying age for state pension credit`
#ASSERT `s 148(2A) the age that paragraph (a) of subsection (2) reads` FALSE EQUALS `s 148(2A) pensionable age`

-- "includes any payment which the Secretary of State accepts as being analogous to it": a payment not accepted
-- is not refused by those words, since "includes" does not close the list.
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The records of terms fixed by another Act or instrument, one each.
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) carer support payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) state pension credit`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002"
#ASSERT (`s 150(2) how the term is defined` `s 150(2) pensionable age`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
